WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.490
Keep honest records, tell stories with care, and check before you forward.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.090
This is the video for module three of Voice Notes, Photos and Videos for Expression.

3
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:17.930
Sometimes media is proof: a payment you made, a promise about a date, or goods that arrived damaged.

4
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.340
Sometimes it keeps a grandmother's voice, or shows what your women's group achieved this year.

5
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:31.760
And when you share widely, two duties come with it. Make sure people can follow it, and make sure it is true.

6
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.710
Start with a wide shot that shows where you are, then the close-up. A close-up alone could have been taken anywhere.

7
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.630
Your phone stores the date and time of each photo. You can see it in Details.

8
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.230
Photograph all sides of a damaged item, all pages of a document, and the packaging and label.

9
00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:00.500
Never crop, filter or add stickers to the original. If you need a cropped version, make a copy.

10
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:07.150
A short narration on the spot, saying the day, the time and what you are showing, adds clarity.

11
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:17.640
For example, Funmi in Lagos paid a carpenter a deposit for a wardrobe. Weeks later, it has not arrived, and he has stopped replying clearly.

12
00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:29.150
She saves the transfer receipt and writes it in her timeline: on 12 March she paid a 50,000 naira deposit, of an agreed 120,000 naira.

13
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:37.990
She finds his voice note promising delivery by 30 March. She exports the chat with its media to her Google Drive.

14
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:48.150
From 30 March to 20 April is 21 days late. She sends him one calm typed message with the dates, and shares the timeline with her estate chairman.

15
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:57.040
Save important media to your gallery, then copy the originals to a backup like Google Drive, in a folder with a clear name.

16
00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:05.370
Share copies, not originals. And do not delete the chat, even if it is upsetting, until the matter is fully settled.

17
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:14.050
Your safety comes first. Never confront an angry person with a camera. If you are in danger, leave and seek help.

18
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:21.890
For any court matter or serious dispute, speak to a lawyer, a legal aid service or a trusted community leader first.

19
00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:36.980
Almost every good short story has three parts. For example, Uche in Owerri tells her cooperative's year in five photos. Before: in January, 8 members with no savings, meeting under a mango tree.

20
00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.500
The turning point: in April, they opened a group account.

21
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:51.070
Then progress: a soap-making training, and a first sale of 60 bars. After: in December, 15 members and their own stall.

22
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.470
Each caption states one fact the photo cannot show. And Uche leaves out any figure she has not checked.

23
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:12.800
When you record an elder, ask first and agree who may listen. Choose a quiet time when she is rested. Ask open questions, like: tell me about your wedding day. Record in parts of 10 to 15 minutes with the voice recorder.

24
00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:24.020
Listen more than you talk, and let silence bring the memories. Never record someone who is distressed. And if a storyteller changes her mind later, respect it.

25
00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:39.620
For example, Rukayat's aunt posts a flood video marked Forwarded many times. Rukayat pauses it and sees shop signs that do not fit their town. Google Lens shows the video is from another country, years earlier.

26
00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:49.000
So run five checks. Who made it? When and where? Does it ask for money or panic? Do trusted sources confirm it? And would sharing hurt someone?

27
00:03:50.250 --> 00:04:02.860
To remember. Keep records clear, dated and unedited. Tell stories in three parts. Describe photos in words and type a summary under voice notes, for people who cannot see or hear well.

28
00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:10.050
And if a voice note sounds like a relative asking urgently for money, call back on the number you already have saved.

29
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:24.770
Now practise. Start one real record with a dated timeline. Record one memory, or tell one story in five photos. And describe three photos, then run the five checks on one forwarded item.

30
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.060
Continue with the lessons below.
